/*
  PDFRenderV - the desktop viewer (absolute application).

  Double-clicking a PDF makes the Filer run Alias$@RunType_ADF, which
  the module points at this small AIF binary (*Run <viewer> file).
  All document work happens in the PDFRenderV module through its
  SWIs; this application is only the window, the toolbar and the
  PDriver print loop.  (An earlier in-module viewer using CMunge's
  module-is-runnable entry died inside Wimp_Initialise on the Kinetic
  Box RO5.31 softload - entering an RMA module as an application is
  broken there, so the viewer became a plain application, which is
  solid everywhere.)

  The viewer opens a scrollable document window with a toolbar pane:
    [<] [page n/N] [>]   [-] [zoom%] [+]   [Print]
  The page is rendered by the same engine the SWIs use, into a 32bpp
  180dpi sprite kept in a dynamic area (so big zooms do not fight the
  CLib heap), and plotted 1:1 pixels on redraw.  Print re-runs the
  renderer inside a PDriver job, so paths and fonts reach the printer
  as vectors, not as a screen dump.

  Wimp/PDriver interfaces per the PRMs: Wimp_CreateWindow block
  (88-byte header + 32-byte icons), pane technique on open events,
  PDriver_SelectJob/GiveRectangle/DrawPage/GetRectangle job loop with
  rectangles in OS units and positions in millipoints.

  Copyright (c) RISC OS Technologies 2026.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: CDDL-1.0
  Licensed under the Common Development and Distribution License 1.0; see LICENSE.
*/

