/* Nested Wimp: R2 of the extended Wimp_OpenWindow, and the nesting
   flags for R4.  Every anchor (bits 16-27) is %01, "link to the left
   or bottom of the parent's visible area" - the bar is pinned to the
   parent's bottom-left corner at a fixed size.                      */
/* --- Toolbox ---------------------------------------------------------

   The window, its toolbar and the gadgets on it come from
   res/Resources,fae rather than being built here.  That is how Select's
   ImageViewer did it, and it is the only way to get the controls it
   had: the arrows either side of the row are Adjuster gadgets and the
   pair beside the page number belong to a NumberRange, and the Toolbox
   draws those from its own resources.  Asking the Wimp for sprites
   called "left" and "right" gets empty boxes - RISC OS 5's pool has no
   such sprites.

   The poll loop stays ours.  Toolbox events arrive through Wimp_Poll
   as event &200 with the event code in the block, so handling them is
   one more case rather than a rewrite into callbacks.              */

#define Toolbox_CreateObject    0x44EC0
#define Toolbox_ShowObject      0x44EC3
#define Toolbox_HideObject      0x44EC4
#define Toolbox_ObjectMiscOp    0x44EC6
